From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 02:53:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] web-app: reply count in message footer opens a
 reply-thread dialog
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Messages that have replies now show a chat-bubble icon plus count next to
the timestamp, in the same shape as the broadcast view counter. Clicking
it opens a Telegram-style thread dialog that renders the whole reply
chain — root message plus nested replies, resolved and sorted by core via
the new getMessageReplyCount/getMessageReplyThread jsonrpc calls — as
regular message bubbles, refreshed on the chat's MsgsChanged events. The
dialog wraps the bubbles in its own ReactionsBarProvider (dialogs render
outside the message list's instance), and jumping to a message from a
quote inside the dialog closes it through the existing __closeAllDialogs
hook, landing in the chat as usual.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
